        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-control-sigma-max>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-mid-stage-critical-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-radial-spectrum-ks-statistic-specimen-vs-simulation>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ratio-sweep-wavelength-slope>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-simulation-gray-level-cv-versus-specimen>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 42 µm on Gasterosteus doryssus_mid (Truckee Fm, 10.01 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 83.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 at the 42 µm detail scale (4.194e-05 m, 10.01 Ma, vestigial spine, T = +9 kyr). The mid-stage fastest mode is 41.94 µm. Predicted neighbours are 32.14 µm (early, full girdle) and 56.90 µm (late, pelvic loss). Analytic versus RK2 dispersion Pearson r = 0.9897, RMSE = 0.070. Equal-diffusion control σ_max = -0.324. Ratio sweep from 12 to 32 lengthens λ. The growth GIF registers that field onto the Voje, Bell & Stuart 2022 plate (12 frames, 640×480) and scores CV similarity 92.3. The unguided stripe field alone is near the 58 CV floor and is not claimed as a skeleton match. Overall 83.8/100. Remediations: Du sensitivity, pure-field CV recorded beside the registered CV, and a bone-versus-sediment radial split. Overall 83.8/100 (faithfulness 82.6, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 78, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/gasterosteus_doryssus_mid_turing_wavelength_s0_growth.gif: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/gif, 2323139 B, 640×480 px, 12 frames, artifact_sha256 101ffda1755cf4e1742f15b040a2a2c4e8e46fafa1f20a7ecbbcb9a7e060dc44 (sha256 101ffda1755cf4e1742f15b040a2a2c4e8e46fafa1f20a7ecbbcb9a7e060dc44), spec_fingerprint dc4c1601bb00a6d80d4baed16fe77c8243511e825b49d7d785e454e5f8378e0b. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: dc4c1601bb00a6d80d4baed16fe77c8243511e825b49d7d785e454e5f8378e0b; artifact_sha256: 101ffda1755cf4e1742f15b040a2a2c4e8e46fafa1f20a7ecbbcb9a7e060dc44; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gasterosteus_doryssus_mid_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_doryssus_mid_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=38c0a5455a7e482a..., datasets/gasterosteus_doryssus_mid_turing_wavelength_s0/gasterosteus_doryssus_mid_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=a1d587e4264868ea...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion: a critical wavenumber selected by diffusion and reaction rates. | Kondo & Asai 1995: reaction-diffusion waves set pigment spacing on fish skin. | Bell & Haglund 1982 and Hunt, Bell & Travis 2008: directional pelvic reduction in Truckee Fm G. doryssus. | Shapiro et al. 2004 and Chan et al. 2010: extant pelvic reduction maps to a Pitx1 enhancer deletion. | Voje, Bell & Stuart 2022: CC BY 4.0 plate of weakly and strongly armored G. doryssus morphs.; reconstructed_in_script: Schnakenberg Jacobian at (a, b) = (0.062, 1.18), σ(k), and Du bisection onto 41.94 µm. | Chronoseries (Dv/Du, γ) = (14.2, 1.55), (18, 1), (24.8, 0.62) giving 32.14, 41.94, 56.90 µm. | Spectral diffusion plus reaction substeps, ratio sweep, equal-diffusion control, RK2 dispersion check.; transfer_boundary: 42 µm melanophore spacing is transferred from extant pigment-pattern RD onto a fossil that preserves bone, not chromatophores.; does_not_claim: That the centimetre-scale fossil photograph is a 42 µm histological section. | That Pitx1 was sequenced from these Miocene fish. | That the unguided stripe field by itself reproduces the skeleton (pure-field CV is about 58).." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Report λ under Du scaled by 0.9 and 1.1 so the 42 µm calibration has an uncertainty band.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Store the unguided pure-field CV next to the registered-render CV instead of only the composite.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Split the fossil plate into bone versus sediment and compare radial spectra inside the bone mask.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.38e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 42 µm on Gasterosteus doryssus_mid (Truckee Fm, 10.01 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "At γ = 1, raising Dv/Du from 12 to 32 lengthens λ_pix from 12.91 to 15.73, monotonically, and every ratio in that list is Turing-unstable. The chronoseries is a different path: γ falls from 1.55 to 0.62 while the ratio rises from 14.2 to 24.8, and λ goes 32.14 → 41.94 → 56.90 µm. Both controls move the wavelength in the direction the dispersion predicts. Du itself is still a solved constant; a ±10% Du probe is not in this pass." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 42 µm on Gasterosteus doryssus_mid (Truckee Fm, 10.01 Ma) — Reproducibility package: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Seed 3230, deterministic 48-step Du bisection, --self-test asserts wavelength order, |λ_mid − 41.94 µm| < 0.05, Pearson r > 0.98, negative control, monotone ratio sweep, growing field variance, and a GIF of at least 10 frames at least 480 px. The self-test passed on 2026-10-27 (r = 0.98974, λ = 32.14/41.94/56.90 µm). Dependencies are the repo scientific stack (numpy, scipy, Pillow, matplotlib). No second machine was used." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 42 µm on Gasterosteus doryssus_mid (Truckee Fm, 10.01 Ma) — Source and data traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Seven DOIs were checked on Crossref on 2026-10-27, including Bell & Haglund 1982 at 10.1017/s0094837300006990 and the plate's source paper 10.1111/jeb.13984. The specimen file is the Wikimedia Commons original, CC BY 4.0, SHA-256 a1d587e4264868ea273dcbf9576536275406dfd0a3e43481c7d879b13d2d19ea, re-checked at runtime. Deduction: author lists for Shapiro 2004 and Chan 2010 are abbreviated in the audit references; the BibTeX file holds the fuller lists." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
