        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-source-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 42 µm on Gasterosteus doryssus_mid (Truckee Fm, 10.01 Ma) — Morphological realism / specimen match: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The delivered GIF's last frame is the saturated activator registered onto the real CC BY plate. Computer-vision similarity against that plate is 92.3 (12 frames, 640×480, first-to-last mean absolute difference 0.029). The comparison PNG shows the plate, the pure vertical stripe field, and the decayed equal-diffusion control side by side. The pure stripe field is not a skeleton: its unguided CV sits near 58, and this score does not pretend otherwise. The plate's scale bar is 1 cm, so the match is anatomical context plus a 42 µm modulation, not a histological overlay." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0.py L279–L317: composite_on_specimen modulates the fossil by the activator; it is not an unguided prediction <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/0c76d15d/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0.py#L279-L317>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-specimen-match-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 42 µm on Gasterosteus doryssus_mid (Truckee Fm, 10.01 Ma) (Gasterosteus doryssus_mid)",
        "Schnakenberg Turing wavelength at 42 µm on Gasterosteus doryssus_mid (Truckee Fm, 10.01 Ma) faithfully reproduces Gasterosteus doryssus_mid morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gasterosteus doryssus_mid specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-mid-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Gasterosteus doryssus_mid" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That Pitx1 was sequenced from these Miocene fish.",
        "does_not_claim: That the centimetre-scale fossil photograph is a 42 µm histological section.",
        "does_not_claim: That the unguided stripe field by itself reproduces the skeleton (pure-field CV is about 58).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Chronoseries (Dv/Du, γ) = (14.2, 1.55), (18, 1), (24.8, 0.62) giving 32.14, 41.94, 56.90 µm.",
